{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the configuration boundary: the initializer takes the Mixpanel settings most apps set at launch, and consent controls are methods on the service. The Mixpanel SDK stays a private implementation detail of this package."}]},{"anchor":"Default-initialization","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Default initialization"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For most apps:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults match the Mixpanel SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelOptions"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushInterval: 60"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"optOutTrackingByDefault: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", gzip on, a random-UUID anonymous ID, "},{"code":"trackAutomaticEvents: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The initializer is the same on every platform."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Mixpanel SDK keys instances by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instanceName"},{"text":" (falling back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"text":"). Constructing a second service with the same name returns the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"existing","type":"text"}]},{"text":" SDK instance, and none of the options passed to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" take effect. The new service is still a separate adapter: settings the adapter applies itself do reach the shared instance, and the state it keeps is its own, not shared with the first service. For example, it writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loggingEnabled: true"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useIPAddressForGeoLocation: false"},{"text":" to the instance. After its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"text":" or opt-in, the instance carries this service’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"superProperties"},{"text":", or none. With ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault: true"},{"text":" and no stored consent choice, it reports ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":", even if the instance is opted in, until a flush it starts on the instance completes, and its consent, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"text":" calls wait for that flush. Construct the service once, where the store is configured — not per view, per preview, or per test.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"serverURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must be an absolute URL with a scheme and host. Requests to anything else fail, and a string that isn’t a URL at all makes every ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" wait out the SDK’s 120-second request timeout. The adapter asserts on this in Debug builds.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"anchor":"EU--India-data-residency","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"EU \/ India data residency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"serverURL:"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    serverURL: \"https:\/\/api-eu.mixpanel.com\"  \/\/ or \"https:\/\/api-in.mixpanel.com\"",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Region is fixed at construction; the service has no per-event region knob.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Opt-out-by-default","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Opt-out by default"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your jurisdiction requires explicit opt-in, construct the service in opted-out mode and hand ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/setOptedOut(_:)"},{"text":" to the plugin as its consent hook:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    optOutTrackingByDefault: true",")","","AnalyticsPlugin(","    state: \\.analytics,","    action: AppAction.analytics,","    extractAction: { if case .analytics(let a) = $0 { a } else { nil } },","    service: service,","    onConsentChange: { await service.setOptedOut($0) }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From then on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send(.analytics(.setOptedOut(_:)))"},{"type":"text","text":" switches both the plugin’s gate and Mixpanel’s own. The plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsState(isOptedOut:)"},{"type":"text","text":" has to start out agreeing with Mixpanel. Either seed it from the consent your app stores and dispatch that value once at launch (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), or seed it from the service:"}]},{"code":["initialState.analytics = AnalyticsState(isOptedOut: service.isOptedOut)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/isOptedOut","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" answers synchronously. On a first launch with "},{"code":"optOutTrackingByDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as soon as the service exists, even if the SDK has not yet applied that default on its own queue."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both directions return only once the SDK has applied them, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatched straight after consent is honored and one dispatched straight after withdrawal is dropped. Mixpanel remembers the choice across launches; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"type":"text","text":" only decides the state before the user has chosen."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opting out deletes whatever is still queued instead of sending it, then clears the local identity, without waiting for the network. An upload that has already started is not cancelled: the SDK checks consent only when a flush starts and between its event and profile queues, so a flush already sending events finishes sending the events it had read. Signing out with ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics(.reset)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is different; it sends the queue first, so events recorded before sign-out keep their user."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opting out does "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" delete the user’s Mixpanel profile or data. The SDK’s own attempt at that is never sent, and the adapter discards it because it would later delete the next user’s profile instead. Erase data with Mixpanel’s GDPR deletion API from your server."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" remain available for apps that don’t route consent through the plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Custom-device-IDs","level":2,"text":"Custom device IDs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default Mixpanel makes the anonymous device ID a random UUID, which does not survive app reinstall. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"useUniqueDistinctId: true"},{"type":"text","text":" swaps it for the device’s own identifier — the IDFV on iOS, but the Mac’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hardware serial number"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on macOS, which most privacy policies won’t allow. If your app maintains its own stable device identity — for example a Keychain-minted UUID hydrated into state at launch — hand it to the SDK with "},{"code":"deviceIdProvider:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Cache the ID at launch; the provider must not do I\/O inline.","let deviceID = keychainStore.value(.deviceID) ?? mintAndStoreDeviceID()","","let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    deviceIdProvider: { deviceID }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK calls the closure synchronously on every launch, on "},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and on opt-out, some of those times while holding its internal lock — so it must be fast: return a cached value, never Keychain or network reads, and never call back into the service or Mixpanel, which deadlocks. Return "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or a blank string to fall back to the SDK default. Returning the same value every call keeps the device ID stable across resets; returning a fresh value gives ephemeral identities."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Adding a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIdProvider"},{"text":" to an app that already shipped with the default device ID changes the anonymous identity on that device. The SDK logs a warning when the provided value differs from the persisted one.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Flush-interval","level":2,"text":"Flush interval"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\", flushInterval: 30)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" disables the timer. The plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" (called on app shutdown) bypasses the interval and sends everything queued, waiting for the network. The SDK sends one request per 50 records, each bounded at 120 seconds, so use the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush(timeout:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on shutdown paths."}]},{"anchor":"Diagnostic-logging","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Diagnostic logging"},{"code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\", loggingEnabled: true)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Turns on the Mixpanel SDK’s logging, which helps when checking an integration during development; leave it off in release builds. The SDK’s logger is shared by every Mixpanel instance in the process, so this turns logging on for all of them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Geo-by-IP","text":"Geo by IP"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-token\", useIPAddressForGeoLocation: false)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops Mixpanel from working out the user’s location from the request’s IP address, for when your privacy policy forbids it."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Aliases-and-ID-merge","text":"Aliases and ID merge"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Projects on Mixpanel’s Simplified ID Merge (check your project’s Identity Merge setting) ignore aliases: "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone links the anonymous device to the signed-in user. Dispatch "},{"code":".analytics(.alias(newID:previousID:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only for projects on Original ID Merge. There, a "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"previousID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" aliases the anonymous distinct ID the device’s events were sent under, and the alias never changes who is identified locally."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Switching-users","level":2,"text":"Switching users"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" moves to a different user, the adapter first sends everything queued for the previous user and waits for it — the SDK otherwise sends every queued profile update under whoever is identified at send time. Dispatching "},{"code":".analytics(.reset)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on sign-out is still the right shape; it also clears super properties set at runtime (the ones passed to the initializer come back automatically)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Update-and-remove-profile-properties","level":2,"text":"Update and remove profile properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property left out of a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" call is not sent, so the value Mixpanel already has stays. To delete a saved property, pass it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".null"},{"type":"text","text":", which sends an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$unset"},{"type":"text","text":" for that key:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Sets `plan` and `experiment_variant`.","await service.identify(","    userID: \"user-1\",","    properties: [\"plan\": .string(\"pro\"), \"experiment_variant\": .string(\"b\")]",")","","\/\/ Updates `plan`. `experiment_variant` keeps its value.","await service.identify(userID: \"user-1\", properties: [\"plan\": .string(\"team\")])","","\/\/ Deletes `experiment_variant`.","await service.identify(userID: \"user-1\", properties: [\"experiment_variant\": .null])"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This holds when the plugin calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" for you: if you drop a key from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" derived from state, the saved value stays. To delete it, map the key to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".null"},{"type":"text","text":". Only a top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".null"},{"type":"text","text":" deletes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each property you pass is sent whole, and the new value replaces the saved one. A null inside an array or dictionary is dropped before sending, so it does not delete anything by itself, but the rest of that value replaces the saved value. If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefs"},{"type":"text","text":" is saved as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{theme: dark}"},{"type":"text","text":" and you identify with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[\"prefs\": .dict([\"theme\": .null])]"},{"type":"text","text":", the adapter sends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefs"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{}"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"theme"},{"type":"text","text":" is gone from the saved value. To keep the other entries of a dictionary, send them again. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ValueTranslation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the translation rules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every "},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the adapter sends also carries the SDK’s own automatic people properties (for example "},{"code":"$ios_device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"$swift_lib_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), except any listed in "},{"code":"excludeProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". They are sent whenever a call has at least one property that is not null. A call whose properties are empty or all null sends no "},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Exclude-properties","level":2,"text":"Exclude properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strip named property keys from outgoing events and People "},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"$set_once","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" updates before the SDK stores or sends them — a construction-time guard against PII leaking through event properties:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"your-token\",","    excludeProperties: [\"email\", \"full_name\"]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded keys are dropped by the Mixpanel SDK itself, so the rule holds no matter which mapper or reducer produced the event. Other People operators ("},{"code":"$add","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$append","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$unset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) pass through unfiltered, and keys Mixpanel requires for ingestion ("},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"token","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) are never stripped even if listed."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Multiple-instances","level":2,"text":"Multiple instances"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your app sends to more than one Mixpanel project, give each a unique "},{"code":"instanceName","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let prodService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"prod-token\",","    instanceName: \"prod\"",")","let internalService = MixpanelAnalyticsService(","    token: \"internal-token\",","    instanceName: \"internal\"",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per service. Each plugin owns its own state slice."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Escape-hatch-build-your-own-MixpanelInstance","level":2,"text":"Escape hatch: build your own `MixpanelInstance`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For configuration the initializer does not surface — "},{"code":"ProxyServerConfig","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", custom delegates, anything that requires direct access to "},{"code":"MixpanelInstance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/init(instance:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Mixpanel  \/\/ only required for this advanced path","","let instance = Mixpanel.initialize(","    options: MixpanelOptions(","        token: \"your-token\",","        proxyServerConfig: myProxyConfig","    )",")","let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(instance: instance)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the only path that requires importing Mixpanel into your app. If you find yourself reaching for it for something common (an SDK knob the initializer should surface), please open an issue — the goal is to keep the happy path Mixpanel-free."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtoimplementservice"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"How to Implement the Service","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure "},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to match your privacy, residency, and batching needs — without ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your app.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/optOutTracking()":{"title":"optOutTracking()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optOutTracking","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optouttracking()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Opts the user out of all tracking, and returns once the SDK has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applied it: from then on ","type":"text"},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","isActive":true},{"text":". Does nothing if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user is already opted out. The choice persists across launches.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optOutTracking()","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optInTracking","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"distinctID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"properties"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"text":"AnalyticsValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SwiduxAnalytics0B5ValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/optintracking(distinctid:properties:)","abstract":[{"text":"Opts the user back into tracking and returns once the SDK has applied","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" issued straight afterwards is honored.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that owns and forwards to a Mixpanel SDK","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mixpanel.initialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"collection","kin